          'Practical consequences: you cannot "command a torso position" the way you command a joint angle; you must generate ground reaction forces and moments that produce the desired base motion. During a swing phase, one foot carries the whole robot, and the contact constraints change discretely - which is why walking controllers are hybrid systems with switching, not smooth regulators.',
